A here, has 3. Contract [1], for 14,250 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not indicate improper conduct. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or multiple separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not prove wrongdoing in procurement processes.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts [1], [2], and [3] to see if they align with the body’s needs. Verify if multiple contracts for similar services were awarded in the same period, which might suggest repeated requests for the same good or service.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["3AkEDyZCbVZrhBlEHQFSKA%3D%3D","WMNGNUNi49W5HQrHoP3G5A%3D%3D","Nap5GyZTQ9EzjChw4z%2FXvw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}